    shadow: 'Their hunger for intensity makes them easy to hook with hot-and-cold treatment, and hard to free from it. A manipulative partner can withhold, provoke and then reward, and the lover of storms experiences this as passion rather than control. Over time the swings can slide into real harm, with jealousy, threats or worse dressed up as proof of love. Meanwhile steady, caring people are pushed away as dull. The audience for the show shrinks to the one person who keeps it going, often the person least worth keeping.',
    honest: 'The need is to feel intensely alive and deeply cared for. Both can be met without chaos: in art, sport or risk that harms no one, and in a love whose depth shows in what it quietly survives rather than in how loudly it breaks.',
